<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Water Inlet Connection: 12 mm press-fit)/Pg 20 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

358 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Drain Line: 12 mm press-fit connection)/Pg 20 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

359 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Boiler Tank: Immersion heater-based, with an automatic water filling system and electrical water level sensor)/Pg 20 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

360 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(This system provides continuous humidity control for prolonged tests.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

361 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The boiler system is constructed with a SS 304-grade tank, integrated with a high-quality immersion heater. The heater meets internal safety standards with a maximum leakage current of 30 mA. The boiler also includes an automatic water filling system, using a GEV \(Germany make\) solenoid valve, along with a water level electronic sensor for reliable and safe operation.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

362 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(DEHUMIDIFICATION SYSTEM :)/E(DEHUMIDIFICATION SYSTEM :)/Pg 20 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

363 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Dehumidification: Controlled via PLC logic, utilizing a solenoid valve and cooling coil to reduce chamber humidity. The chamber automatically adjusts humidity levels using a sophisticated dehumidification system integrated with the refrigeration system.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

364 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The dehumidification system is controlled via PLC logic. It operates through a de-humidity solenoid valve, integrated with the refrigeration system. The cooling coil contains a refrigeration cold tube that absorbs moisture from the chamber's air. The system monitors the cold tube temperature through the PLC. When dehumidification is required, the cold tube captures the moisture, freezes it into water particles, and drains the condensed water, effectively reducing the chamber's internal humidity.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

365 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Condensation Protection and Advanced Dehumidification System)/Pg 20 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

366 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Our test chamber is designed to provide reliable condensation protection and precise humidity control, ensuring optimal testing conditions for sensitive specimens. Key features include:)/Pg 20 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

367 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Condensation Protection with Separate Dehumidifying Coil:)/Pg 20 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

368 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The test chamber is equipped with a separate dehumidifying coil that effectively removes moisture from the air, minimizing the risk of condensation on the test specimen.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

369 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(This dedicated coil helps maintain the integrity of the testing environment, ensuring accurate and reliable test results without unwanted moisture affecting the specimen.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

370 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(ADVANCED DEHUMIDIFICATION AND HUMIDITY CONTROL SYSTEM :)/E(ADVANCED DEHUMIDIFICATION AND HUMIDITY CONTROL SYSTEM :)/Pg 21 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

371 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(RTD Sensor for Tube Skin Temperature Control:)/Pg 21 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

372 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 700 0 R/E(An RTD sensor is placed on the dehumidifying refrigeration copper tube coil to monitor and maintain the tube\220s skin temperature.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

373 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 701 0 R/E(The sensor value can be easily adjusted through the HMI interface, allowing users to set and control the desired temperature and dehumidification levels with precision.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

374 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 702 0 R/E(This ensures consistent regulation of humidity levels within the chamber by controlling the refrigerant flow via the solenoid valve.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

375 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Solenoid Valve Regulation:)/Pg 21 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

376 0 obj
